.Dd April 30, 2026
.Dt OS_CROSS_ARCH_IS_SUPPORTED 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm os_cross_arch_is_supported
.Nd determine if cross-architecture compatibility is supported
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In os/arch/arm64.h
.Ft bool
.Fn os_cross_arch_is_supported "os_cross_arch_t arch"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn os_cross_arch_is_supported
function returns whether the kernel provides the set of
cross-architecture compatibility features required by a user-space
compatibility layer to run processes built for the CPU architecture
identified by
.Fa arch
via translation.
.Pp
A
.Dv true
return value does not imply that any particular compatibility
layer is installed, enabled, or functional on the running system;
it only reports whether the underlying kernel features that such a
layer depends on are present.
.Pp
The
.Fa arch
argument must be one of the following constants:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv OS_CROSS_ARCH_X86_64
The x86_64 (Intel/AMD 64-bit) architecture.
.El
.Pp
Any other value of
.Fa arch ,
including values that may be defined by future SDKs but are not
recognized by the running system, causes the function to return
.Dv false .
.Pp
The return value is constant for the lifetime of the system and may be
safely cached by callers.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn os_cross_arch_is_supported
function returns
.Dv true
if cross-architecture compatibility for
.Fa arch
is supported, or
.Dv false
otherwise.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sysctl 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn os_cross_arch_is_supported
function first appeared in macOS 26.6.
